[Term]
id: UBERON:0000950
name: gracilis
def: "The most superficial muscle on the medial side of the thigh. It is thin and flattened, broad above, narrow and tapering below. It arises by a thin aponeurosis from the anterior margins of the lower half of the symphysis pubis and the upper half of the pubic arch." [Wikipedia:Gracilis_muscle]
